    "387": {
      "date": "2026-10-01",
      "edition": "Thursday 1 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Ranking stat",
          "heading": "France record one-week tenure as longest unbroken spell at world number one",
          "body": "France’s tenure at the summit of the world rankings remains a remarkably brief historical footnote. Their longest unbroken spell at No. 1 in the world lasted just one week, occurring in July 2022. While Les Bleus have established themselves as perennial contenders, securing two wins from three in the current Nations Championship, they have yet to find the sustained dominance required to lock down the top spot. Following their 42-15 victory over Japan, Fabien Galthié’s men remain third in the international standings."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Scotland wing Darcy Graham ruled out for remainder of year",
          "body": "Wallabies name Toby Macpherson in 34-man Bledisloe Cup squad."
