    "391": {
      "date": "2026-10-01",
      "edition": "Thursday 1 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "HERITAGE INSPIRATION",
          "heading": "Josh Adams and Alex Mann draw inspiration from archives before autumn tests",
          "body": "Cardiff duo Josh Adams and Alex Mann have visited the national archives to study historic jerseys as Wales begin preparations for the autumn Nations Championship. The collection, curated by heritage expert Peter Owens, features memorabilia from previous fixtures against Japan, New Zealand and Australia. The Cardiff wing, currently sidelined from club duties through injury, described the experience as a reminder that the squad plays for \"the community, for the history, for the heritage.\" Mann highlighted the grit of past generations who balanced tests with full-time jobs."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Scotland wing Darcy Graham ruled out for remainder of year",
