      "edition": "Thursday 1 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "SCORING RECORDS",
          "heading": "Argentina achieve 52-point scoring high in away win over Wales",
          "body": "Argentina’s 52-28 victory over Wales in November 2025 stands as the side’s largest win across their last 11 international matches. During this window, the team has scored a total of 321 points, averaging 29.2 per game. Despite this offensive production, the defence has conceded 346 points at an average of 31.5. These performance metrics define the recent run of form for Felipe Contepomi’s squad as they prepare to return to international action against Ireland."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Scotland wing Darcy Graham ruled out for remainder of year",
